# RELEASE Pipeline

When the user says **RELEASE** (or asks to build and release), run the full pipeline without skipping steps.

## 1. App repo (`localrecord`)

1. Ensure all code changes are complete and `cargo check --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` passes (or rely on CI if cross-compile unavailable locally).
2. Bump `version` in `Cargo.toml` (patch unless user specifies otherwise).
3. Update `README.md` if user-facing behavior changed.
4. Commit and push to `main`.
5. Create and push an annotated tag: `git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "..." && git push origin vX.Y.Z`
6. Wait for `.github/workflows/release.yml` to finish (Windows build + GitHub Release upload).
7. Edit the GitHub release notes with a short changelog (fixes/features since last tag).

## 2. Landing page (`localrecord-landing`)

1. Update `index.html` copy if features or install steps changed.
2. Download links use `release.js` + GitHub API — no manual version strings in hrefs.
3. Commit and push to `main`.
4. Deploy: `vercel --prod --yes` from the landing repo.
5. Point custom domain: `vercel alias set <deployment-url> localrecord.doublea.engineering`

## 3. Verify

- Latest release: `gh release list -R AntoineArt/localrecord --limit 1`
- Asset present: `localrecord-X.Y.Z.exe` and `localrecord-X.Y.Z-x86_64-linux` on the new tag
- Site live: https://localrecord.doublea.engineering shows updated version via `release.js`

